          "text": "{\"schema_version\":\"ai-evaluator-v2/1.1\",\"case_id\":\"9-6\",\"candidate_id\":\"candidate_2\",\"action_assessment\":{\"status\":\"preserved\",\"summary\":\"Most source activities are represented with acceptable paraphrase/grouping: locate/distribute designs, parallel departmental review-plan-revise-test work, cross-department notification, combine/test, and send to manufacturing.\"},\"flow_assessment\":{\"status\":\"preserved\",\"summary\":\"The represented action order is largely preserved: distribution precedes parallel department work, each department follows review -> plan -> revise -> test, and combination/testing occurs after both branches reach completion. The main problems are restart/termination behaviors rather than simple precedence reversals.\"},\"control_flow_assessment\":{\"status\":\"defect\",\"summary\":\"Core control behavior is wrong: failed departmental tests terminate instead of looping back through the department cycle, successful updates only notify the other branch without actually interrupting/restarting it, and combined-test failure terminates instead of starting another design cycle.\"},\"main_error_type\":\"mixed_or_cascading\",\"explanation\":\"The source describes an iterative parallel co-design process with three central control behaviors: departmental test failure must restart that department's cycle, a successful update in one department must interrupt and restart the other department's in-progress work, and combined-design failure must send both designs into another design cycle. The generated graph preserves many activity labels and basic local ordering, but it converts all three restart/recurrence behaviors into dead-end or non-operative paths: departmental failures go to a review action and then end, cross-department 'restart' is only a notification with no restart path, and combined-test failure goes to an action and then ends. As a result, the graph models a mostly one-pass process rather than the required iterative interruptible coordination process.\",\"overall_score\":0.39,\"severity\":\"major\",\"confidence\":\"high\",\"ambiguity_flag\":false,\"ambiguity_explanation\":\"\",\"requires_human_review\":false,\"review_reason\":\"\"}"
        }
